# GINVIFY — PROJECT CONTEXT (ALWAYS APPLIED)

Full spec lives at `/ginvify-website-spec.md`. This rule is a compressed reminder
of the parts that must never be violated, regardless of which phase we're in.
When in doubt, re-read the relevant numbered section of the spec file.

## Brand

- Company: GINVIFY. Core idea: "Engineering Intelligence." / "From Ideas to
  Intelligent Systems."
- Positioning: technology company — Web Applications, AI Engineering, AI
  Agents, Automation, SaaS Platforms, Landing Pages, Digital Products.
- Never invent clients, awards, revenue, employee counts, project counts, or
  testimonials. Conceptual/experimental work must be labeled CONCEPT /
  EXPERIMENT / PROTOTYPE.

## Visual direction (non-negotiable)

- Dark premium tech aesthetic. Background near-black/charcoal
  (`#050607`, `#0A0D10`, `#11161A`). Accents: lime `#B7FF3C`, cyan `#5CE1E6`.
- Do not overuse gradients. Rely on typography, negative space, motion, depth.
- Must NOT look like: generic AI startup, generic SaaS template, generic
  Tailwind landing page, random rotating-sphere website, neon cyberpunk,
  crypto site, gaming site, or a site with a mascot slapped everywhere.
- Target feel: "Apple-level restraint + creative WebGL studio + AI
  engineering laboratory."

## The signature system — treat as ONE object, not many

- The brand signature is the G-logo → particle → network morph (spec
  Section 5A). The Hero's "Digital Intelligence Core" IS this object.
- Every homepage section (Services, AI, Automation, Engineering, Technology)
  must reuse and reshape the SAME underlying particle/node system — never
  spin up an unrelated 3D scene per section. If a task seems to need a new
  3D object for a new section, stop and ask whether it should instead be a
  new *state* of `IntelligenceCore`.
- The story closes by converging the network back into the G before the
  final "LET'S BUILD WHAT'S NEXT." section.

## The mascot — scope is intentionally tiny

- `components/mascot/GinvifyCat.tsx` is a small, quiet, line-art cat. It is
  NEVER used in the hero, the main scroll story, Services/AI/Automation/
  Technology/Engineering sections, or navigation.
- Approved locations only: 404/error page, empty states, a small footer
  easter egg, optional lightweight loading state on non-critical pages.
- No mascot dialogue, no puns, no "mascot voice" in copy near it.

## Phase discipline — the most important rule in this file

- We build in 4 phases (spec Section 31). Only work on the CURRENT phase
  unless explicitly told otherwise. Do not add pages, sections, or features
  that belong to a later phase, even if it seems convenient to do while
  "already in there."
- Phase 1 (Design system, Typography, Nav, Hero, Intelligence Core +
  G-signature, Scroll engine) is the quality gate for the whole project.
  Never sacrifice Phase-1 polish to rush toward more content.
- If a request is ambiguous about which phase it belongs to, ask before
  building.

## Engineering baseline

- Stack: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Three.js, React Three Fiber, Drei,
  GSAP + ScrollTrigger, Lenis, Tailwind CSS.
- No giant single components — separate UI / animation logic / Three.js
  scene / mascot / content / localization (spec Section 27).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` everywhere motion is added.
- Every animation must communicate something (transformation, intelligence,
  connection, flow, architecture, scale, automation) — never animation for
  its own sake (spec Section 29).
